>>
Rule 1 (integer axis must be within valid range)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : int} |= v_2 ≥ 0 - ndim(v_1) ∧ v_2 ≤ ndim(v_1) - 1
>>
Rule 2 (only valid integer axes for 1-D tensors)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : int} |= if ndim(v_1) = 1 then (v_2 = 0 ∨ v_2 = -1)
>>
Rule 3 (tuple axis: non-empty, size bounded by rank, and each index in range)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tuple(int)} |= v_2.len ≥ 1 ∧ v_2.len ≤ ndim(v_1) ∧ ∀i ∈ [0, v_2.len - 1] : (v_2[i] ≥ 0 - ndim(v_1) ∧ v_2[i] ≤ ndim(v_1) - 1)
>>
Rule 5 (list axis: non-empty, size bounded by rank, and each index in range)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : list(int)} |= v_2.len ≥ 1 ∧ v_2.len ≤ ndim(v_1) ∧ ∀i ∈ [0, v_2.len - 1] : (v_2[i] ≥ 0 - ndim(v_1) ∧ v_2[i] ≤ ndim(v_1) - 1)
